course: dictionary
lesson: 8488
title: Sandpaper: a thing and an action
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sandpaper is paper with sand or grit stuck to one side. You rub it on wood or other surfaces to make them smooth. The words around it show you which job the word is doing in a sentence.
explain: «Shark skin is covered in tiny tooth-like scales, which feel smooth one way and like sandpaper the other.» Feel, smooth and rough are the clues. Here sandpaper describes how a surface can feel, so it means rough and scratchy.
explain: Sandpaper can also be a verb, a doing word: to sandpaper something means to smooth it by rubbing it with sandpaper. Test your meaning: put «rub with sandpaper» into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Sandpaper is a noun when it names the paper, as in «a sheet of sandpaper».
fact: To sandpaper means to smooth something by rubbing it with sandpaper.
fact: «Rough as sandpaper» is a phrase that means very rough to touch.
fact: In design and technology, you sandpaper wood before you paint it.
fact: In science, sandpaper is used to show friction, the force that slows things that rub together.
exercise: Before painting the shelf, Ruby must «sandpaper the edges». What does she do? | To wash the shelf with water | To cut the edges off with scissors | To paint the edges bright red | *To smooth the edges by rubbing them with sandpaper
exercise: «Shark skin ... feel smooth one way and like sandpaper the other.» What does sandpaper tell you about the skin on that side? | *It feels rough | It has a bright colour | It is very wet | It feels soft and warm
exercise: Tom says, «Sandpaper on a cricket ball breaks the rules.» What is the sandpaper in this sentence? | A soft ball | A rule book | *Rough paper with grit stuck to one side | A kind of cricket bat
test: «Rub the wood with fine sandpaper until it feels smooth.» What must you do? | Put it in water | Wrap it up in a cloth | Cover it with paint | *Rub it smooth with sandpaper
test: Which sentence uses sandpaper as a noun? | «He will sandpaper it later.» | «They sandpapered it twice.» | *«She bought a sheet of sandpaper.» | «She sandpapered the chair.»
exam: Mia says, «My cheek feels like sandpaper after the wind.» What does she mean? | *It feels rough and scratchy | It feels smooth and soft | It feels hot and sticky | It feels wet and cold
